menu "DragonBreath Wi-Fi defaults"

    choice DB_DEFAULT_AP_MODE
        prompt "Setup AP mode for a device with no stored AP mode"
        default DB_DEFAULT_AP_MODE_ALWAYS
        help
            The setup AP mode that a device uses when NVS has no AP mode
            (a new device, a device that never changed the AP mode, or a device
            after a front-panel or factory reset). A stored user choice always
            wins. With no saved Wi-Fi credentials, the setup AP is always on,
            whatever this mode is.

            ALWAYS (default) does not write NVS: dc_wifi uses its own default.
            The other choices write the "ap_mode" NVS key once, before
            dc_wifi_start().

        config DB_DEFAULT_AP_MODE_ALWAYS
            bool "Always: the setup AP stays on next to the Wi-Fi station"
        config DB_DEFAULT_AP_MODE_TEMP
            bool "Temporary: the setup AP stays on for 15 minutes after boot"
        config DB_DEFAULT_AP_MODE_FALLBACK
            bool "Fallback: the setup AP starts only if the station cannot join"
        config DB_DEFAULT_AP_MODE_OFF
            bool "Off: no setup AP while credentials are stored"
            help
                If the station cannot join, there is no setup AP. To recover,
                hold Power + Auto for 5 s, or erase NVS over USB.
    endchoice

endmenu
